 3. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 The maiden flight. Photo: Courtesy of Embraer

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🇧🇷 The first Gripen E fighter produced by Embraer in Brazil has taken flight. The aircraft departed the company's facilities in Gavião Peixoto.

 Why it matters: A contract signed with Brazil in 2014 covered the development and production of 36 Gripens, including 28 single-seater E variants. 💭 My thought bubble: I've followed Embraer closely. More on the aerospace company here and here and here . 📑 Striveworks announced a five-year, $200 million contract for further work on the Army's Next-Generation Command and Control effort. The company is building the baseline AI layer.

 Why it matters: A lot rides on NGC2 and its success (i.e., you can't win if you can't communicate). 💭 My thought bubble: The Army in its recent budget request sought some $4 billion for NGC2 development and delivery. 💵 Fortastra raised $30 million. The Series A was led by First In. Other backers include ATX Ventures, Side Door Ventures and Space Capital.

 Why it matters: At a time when the Pentagon is openly talking about space weapons, this startup is billing itself as a "developer of maneuverable, resilient spacecraft for on-orbit security and national defense." 💭 My thought bubble: My colleague Natalie Breymeyer has a great rundown on defense-tech deals. Give it a read ! 
 
